# Documented, justified exceptions to the backend's blocking Trivy gate (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml). This file is empty by default - the backend
# dependency tree is currently clean of known HIGH/CRITICAL findings.
#
# Add an exception only when a HIGH/CRITICAL finding genuinely cannot be
# remediated immediately (no fixed version yet, or a fix requires a breaking
# change tracked separately) AND it has been reviewed and approved. Each
# entry must document:
#   - the CVE/advisory ID
#   - why it doesn't apply or can't be fixed yet
#   - who approved it and when
#   - a review/expiry date so it doesn't silently become permanent
#
# Example:
# CVE-2025-00000 exp:2026-06-30
# # Transitive via spring-boot-starter-foo; no fixed version upstream yet.
# # Not reachable: the vulnerable code path (XML entity expansion) is never
# # invoked by this app's JSON-only API. Approved by <name> on 2026-01-15,
# # re-review before expiry.
